From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: Recolour the Light visual style to Stained Glass purple

Wine's built-in "Light" visual style (light.msstyles) accents controls, the
selection, focus and window buttons in Windows-10 blue. Stained Glass OS uses a
purple accent everywhere else (the taskbar, Start menu, caption buttons); the
themed common controls were the last blue surface. This recolours the theme's
source SVGs so buttons, checkboxes, radio buttons, sliders, the selection and
the rest carry the project's purple instead:

  #3096fa (accent)      -> #7b2fbe   (Stained Glass purple)
  #2979ff (accent dark) -> #5f2496
  #e3f2fd (accent tint) -> #f0e9fa

The .bmp/.cur/.ico the theme actually packs are generated from these SVGs by
tools/buildimage; build.sh regenerates them after applying the series (it needs
rsvg-convert, icotool and ImageMagick, added to `make deps'). The greys, the
red Close highlight and all non-accent colours are unchanged, so only the blue
becomes purple.
